    "description": "Which side of the anchor element to align the popup against. May automatically change to avoid collisions.",
    "name": "side",
    "origin": "base-ui",
    "required": false,
    "type": ""top" | "bottom" | "left" | "right" | "inline-end" | "inline-start"",
  },
  {
    "default": "0",
    "description": "Distance between the anchor and the popup in pixels. Also accepts a function that returns the distance to read the dimensions of the anchor and positioner elements, along with its side and alignment.

The function takes a \`data\` object parameter with the following properties: - \`data.anchor\`: the dimensions of the anchor element with properties \`width\` and \`height\`. - \`data.positioner\`: the dimensions of the positioner element with properties \`width\` and \`height\`. - \`data.side\`: which side of the anchor element the positioner is aligned against. - \`data.align\`: how the positioner is aligned relative to the specified side.",
    "name": "sideOffset",
    "origin": "base-ui",
    "required": false,
    "type": "number | OffsetFunction",
  },
  {
    "default": "'center'",
    "description": "How to align the popup relative to the specified side.",
    "name": "align",
    "origin": "base-ui",
    "required": false,
    "type": ""center" | "start" | "end"",
  },
  {
    "default": "0",
    "description": "Additional offset along the alignment axis in pixels. Also accepts a function that returns the offset to read the dimensions of the anchor and positioner elements, along with its side and alignment.

The function takes a \`data\` object parameter with the following properties: - \`data.anchor\`: the dimensions of the anchor element with properties \`width\` and \`height\`. - \`data.positioner\`: the dimensions of the positioner element with properties \`width\` and \`height\`. - \`data.side\`: which side of the anchor element the positioner is aligned against. - \`data.align\`: how the positioner is aligned relative to the specified side.",
    "name": "alignOffset",
    "origin": "base-ui",
    "required": false,
    "type": "number | OffsetFunction",
  },
  {
    "default": "'clipping-ancestors'",
